3. Scale up - www.foobar.com

Flow: DNS points to the load balancer cluster. Two HAProxy instances run as a
cluster and both receive traffic. They forward requests to the web server, which
serves static content and passes dynamic requests to the application server, which
queries the database server.

Why each additional element:
- 1 more server: needed so each component can live on its own machine.
- Second load balancer (HAProxy) configured as a cluster with the first one: removes
  the load balancer SPOF. Both nodes check each other with a heartbeat; if one fails,
  the other keeps handling all the traffic.
- Split components (web server, application server, database), each on its own
  server:
  - Web server (Nginx): handles HTTP connections and static files only.
  - Application server: runs only the code base and business logic.
  - Database server (MySQL): runs only the database, with all of that machine's
    memory and disk for data.
  Each layer gets its own resources, a failure in one does not take down the others,
  and each layer can be scaled on its own (for example, adding more application
  servers without touching the database).
